{
  "slug": "signoz",
  "name": "SigNoz",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Official SigNoz plugin for MCP setup, docs, queries, dashboards, and alerts",
  "longDescription": "Ships **13 skills**, **2 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (13): `signoz-creating-alerts` (Create a new SigNoz alert rule from a natural-language intent: threshold, anomaly, log-volume, error-rate, latency, or absent-data alerts…), `signoz-creating-dashboards` (Create a new SigNoz dashboard from a natural-language intent: import a curated template (PostgreSQL, Redis, JVM, k8s, hostmetrics,…), `signoz-explaining-alerts` (Describe what an existing SigNoz alert rule does in plain language: the signal it watches, the threshold and…), `signoz-explaining-dashboards` (Explain what an existing SigNoz dashboard shows in plain operational language: the panels, queries, variables, and what to…), `signoz-generating-queries` (Generate, write, or run an ad-hoc query against SigNoz observability data (metrics, logs, or traces) without wrapping it…), `signoz-investigating-alerts` (Diagnose why a SigNoz alert fired by correlating the alert's own signal with neighbor signals (error rate, latency,…), `signoz-managing-views` (Use when the user wants to create, list, get, update, rename, or delete a SigNoz saved Explorer view), `signoz-mcp-setup` (Initialize or repair SigNoz MCP server configuration for Agent Plugins v1, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, VS Code/GitHub Copilot,…), and 5 more\n- **Hooks** (2): `PreToolUse`, `SessionStart`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `mcp`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install signoz@knowledge-work-plugins` from `SigNoz/agent-skills` (`plugins/signoz`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
